/*
 * Declares the CmpFloatOperatorValue class.
 *
 * CmpFloatOperatorValue represents binary comparison operations applied to two
 * floating-point operands. Floating-point comparisons follow IEEE-754
 * semantics, including NaN propagation rules and the distinction between
 * ordered and unordered comparisons. The result of any comparison is always a
 * boolean value.
 *
 * Typical comparisons include:
 *   - equality / inequality,
 *   - relational comparisons (<, <=, >, >=),
 *   - ordered vs. unordered checks depending on the operator set.
 *   
 * <hr>
 * 
 * @Package: ymirc        
 * @Module: ymirc::semantic::generator::value::operator::binary::float_::cmp
 * @File: ymirc/semantic/generator/value/operator/binary/float_/cmp.yr
 * @Author(s):
